{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.DescentCondition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.DescentCondition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.descent_condition_global","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.descent_condition_global","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L93-L100","doc":"If all obstructions vanish, the distributional connection is\nglobally consistent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.global_iff_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.global_iff_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Global consistency ↔ vanishing obstruction:\nA_∞ is globally well-defined iff κ_n = 0 for all n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.GloballyConsistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.GloballyConsistent","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The distributional connection is globally consistent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.obstruction","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The obstruction class κ_n extracted from the twisted cocycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.addComm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.addComm","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The obstruction space is an additive abelian group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.ObstructionSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.ObstructionSpace","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The obstruction space (H²(𝒮, ℬ)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.cocycleData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.cocycleData","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The twisted cocycle data at each level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.grp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.grp","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Each level carries a group structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.G","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The group of transition functions at each brane level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.DescentCondition","kind":"structure","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L65-L89","doc":"**Descent condition**: when the twisted 2-cocycle condition holds\nat all levels of the brane tower, the distributional connection\n`A_∞` is globally consistent.\n\nThis is the categorical formulation: the obstruction class\n`κ_n ∈ H²(𝒮, ℬ)` is the cohomology class of the twisted cocycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.twisted_cocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.twisted_cocycle","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The twisted cocycle condition:\n`a_{ij} · g_{ijk} · a_{jk}⁻¹ = coboundary(g)_{ijk}`.\nHere we state it as: the conjugation by `a` maps the deviation\nto its coboundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.twoMorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.twoMorphism","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The 2-morphisms (quantum deformation feedback). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.cech","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.cech","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The underlying Čech cocycle data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.TwistedCocycleCondition","kind":"structure","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L43-L63","doc":"**Twisted 2-cocycle condition**.\n\nThe coboundary of the deviation `g_{ijk}` is twisted by the\nquantum deformation 2-morphisms `a_{ij}`:\n`d(g_{ijk}) = a_{ij} · g_{ijk} · a_{jk}⁻¹`.\n\nWhen this holds, the distributional connection `A_∞` is globally\nconsistent — the local deformations glue into a well-defined sheaf. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.deviation_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.deviation_eq","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The deviation is computed from transition functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.deviation","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The 1-cocycle deviation `g_{ijk} = g_{ij} · g_{jk} · g_{ik}⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.transition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.transition","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Transition functions `g_{ij}` on double intersections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.numPatches","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.numPatches","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Index set for the covering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.CechCocycleData","kind":"structure","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-condition.lean#L26-L41","doc":"**Čech cocycle data** at brane level `n`.\n\nOn a triple intersection `U_i ∩ U_j ∩ U_k`, the transition\nfunctions `g_{ij}` form a 1-cocycle up to a coboundary measured\nby the deviation `g_{ijk} = g_{ij} · g_{jk} · g_{ik}⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}